WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.740
- So Exactly what is Drew's News?

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:07.930
We like to say it's the
news served sunny side up.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.390
So let's see what made the papers.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.260
Okay, first up, this
summer, I was really honored

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.160
to be on the cover of InStyle Magazine.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.660
And my old friend, Laura Brown,

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.910
who's the editor-in-chief
allowed me to wear

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.130
one of my personal vintage
T-shirts on the cover.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.533
Fun fact, magazines make money

00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:28.270
by featuring designers on their covers.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.478
And it's a form of advertising
and revenue for them.

00:00:31.478 --> 00:00:35.530
But we got to break the rules

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:38.500
by wearing this Detroit News T-shirt.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.500
After that, the Detroit News
saw this and reissued them,

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.960
'cause they weren't making these anymore,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.250
as a part of a fundraising effort

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.300
for Detroit area college scholarships.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.430
Well, yesterday the Detroit
News itself reported

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:57.238
that sales of the shirt
have raised over $70,000!

00:00:57.238 --> 00:00:59.490
(audience cheers)

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:03.780
I mean, things are possible.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.740
That's what the evidence of this is.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.610
So if you'd like to contribute,

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.450
head over to our website for a link.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.500
And all the proceeds go directly

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.480
to the Rosa L. Parks
Scholarship Foundation.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.600
So let's do this, let's raise
more money, do some good.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.494
This is evidence, it's happening.

00:01:19.494 --> 00:01:21.083
(audience cheers)

00:01:21.083 --> 00:01:23.960
Okay, now seriously, I don't like to get

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.840
into controversial items on Drew's News,

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.310
but I'm gonna have to tackle
this next issue head on.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.300
It's a debate that's gone
viral this week on Twitter,

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.540
and it continues to heat
up more and more each day.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.160
And the question is, if a giraffe

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.650
were to wear a bow tie,
where would the bow tie go?

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:41.110
I'm vacillating.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.470
I think we can all agree it
just looks better up top,

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.200
a pop up color to accentuate the eyes.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.430
But if you think about
it, humans wear a bow tie

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:50.560
at the bottom of their
neck as part of the outfit.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.761
Okay, we have some opposing views

00:01:52.761 --> 00:01:56.060
with our virtual friends, David and Alex.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.080
You have varying opinions,
let's hear them out loud.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.494
David, you go first.

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:00.340
(audience cheers)

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.320
- Well Drew, I gotta say,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.610
I think the bow tie goes
up closer to the top.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:05.240
Just makes more sense there.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.260
- [Drew] Yeah, I hear you.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.143
Alex, rebuttal.

00:02:08.143 --> 00:02:11.007
- Hi Drew, sorry, I'm just
really excited to talk to you.

00:02:11.007 --> 00:02:13.223
- Oh, I'm excited to talk to you too.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.810
- But I actually feel

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.640
very confident answering this question.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.884
I am a designer in the fashion industry.

00:02:21.884 --> 00:02:24.000
So-
- An authority.

00:02:25.855 --> 00:02:28.150
- (laughs) I personally have never

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:31.320
seen anybody wear a bow
tie under their chin,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.570
I don't know about David.

00:02:33.727 --> 00:02:36.990
But I personally believe that it needs

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.450
to be down by the shoulders,
if it is worn properly.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.470
- I hear you both, it's a tough call,

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.790
but I'm gonna go with my
gut on this one, either way.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.890
Giraffes should wear bow
ties, wherever they want.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.060
They're stylish and plain old fun.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.690
Okay, you do you, giraffes.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.010
And thanks, Alex and
David, you're the best.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.640
All right, debate settled.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.330
Finally, it's no secret
we love good news here.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.440
And this story is a perfect example

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.560
of the good we need in the world.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.040
Tyler and Melanie are
newlyweds from Parma, Ohio.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.620
And they had to cancel their wedding

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.830
because of everything that's happening.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.850
And rather than get a
refund for all the catering,

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:18.360
they decided to donate the
food to a local shelter.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.890
And it is so wonderful, we
just had to talk to them.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:23.922
So hello, Tyler and Melanie.

00:03:23.922 --> 00:03:24.755
(audience cheers)

00:03:24.755 --> 00:03:25.820
Thank you for coming on the show!

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.762
- Well, we're excited to
be here, this is crazy.

00:03:31.762 --> 00:03:33.320
- I just wanna say, we kinda match.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.520
- Oh, by the way, totally do.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.420
In fact, we're kind of wearing bows,

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.154
if you get what I'm saying, everyone.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:42.220
- They're lower, though.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.650
- I didn't even realize this.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.470
Okay, this is all so
serendipitous, all right.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:50.053
Well, and before we get into
the amazing thing that you did,

00:03:50.053 --> 00:03:52.334
I just have to know how you guys met.

00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:55.969
- So we actually met at
our friend's wedding.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:58.070
We were partnered up.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.600
I kinda feel like they
did that on purpose.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.210
But we actually had a moment during it.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:06.810
We were taking pictures,
and I fell into him,

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.850
and we kind of both just stood there.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.230
And I think at that moment
we both kinda were like,

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.220
oh, we kind of have this spark.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.070
So we went with it, and here we are.

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.600
- Do you know?

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.950
Oh sorry, go ahead.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.740
- No, no, no, I was just gonna
say it was a magical moment.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.003
It truly was.

00:04:25.048 --> 00:04:26.960
- Do you know how many
people like get dressed up

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.410
and go to a wedding with
so much hope, you know?

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.240
I mean, you guys are kind of proving

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.820
that things are really possible
and to keep hope alive.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:36.400
Okay, so rather than
canceling the catering,

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.740
you donated this to a local shelter.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.800
Why did you do this?

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.001
- Oh, I mean we were working

00:04:43.001 --> 00:04:46.010
with the caterer for quite some time.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.730
And we've gotten to be

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:49.320
pretty good friends with them, actually.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.800
And when COVID hit, all
the local businesses

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:55.490
started to really take a hit.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:58.830
And we felt terrible that
they were going to lose out.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.840
So every year we donate somewhere,

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.690
typically around Christmas, to children,

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:08.050
to get different gifts for
them for underprivileged.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:12.670
So the way things lined
up, it just seemed right

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.820
for us to donate the food
and help somebody out.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.930
- I think you guys are just so amazing.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.350
And I heard a rumor that
you bought a new house?

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:25.370
- We did, we've been here
for like three months now.

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.780
It's a little bit of a fixer upper.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.240
We had to paint this whole room.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.520
It was wonderful.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.539
But yeah, we're really excited.

00:05:33.539 --> 00:05:35.510
Our neighbors are amazing.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:38.070
They have babies, so we
get to play with them.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.400
It's so much fun, so.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.810
- Well, this is perfect,

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.690
because I wanted to
give you a wedding gift.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.650
We are gonna give you a...

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.680
I love design so much.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.380
I have a furniture company
called Flower Home.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:55.770
And today we wanna gift you a
$5,000 credit for Flower Home.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:57.200
So you can get anything you want

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.320
as you begin your life together.

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:03.450
And if you want, Anna and Francesca,

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:04.920
who are the creative directors,

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.260
and I design everything with,

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.240
they're the coolest women,

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.280
we are all gonna personally help you

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.030
put it together to make
your space perfect.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:15.380
So thank you for being here
and sharing your story.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.790
- I don't cry normally, so here I am.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.330
- Thanks you guys so much.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.310
Tyra Banks is next.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.860
We'll be right back, thank you.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.079
We wanna make your dream home.

00:06:26.079 --> 00:06:28.662
(upbeat music)

